{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule","id":1047633,"title":"The Ecstatic Wind [House Rule]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-12T03:32:21-08:00","id":1047633,"title":"The Ecstatic Wind [House Rule]","content":"The Astral Plane supports only self-aware consciousness until the Anima Mundi. The Dreamtime doesn\u2019t array itself according to sapient, dialectical thought. Without some form of protection, differences between a mage\u2019s mind and body or his self-identity and the region erode. This can reduce the traveler to an animalistic state or mutate the mage\u2019s astral form. In extreme cases, transformations actually manifest on the physical plane. Mages leave the Anima Mundi with everything from bestial features to impossible melds of flesh and metal.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen a mage crosses the Omphalos, he confronts the Ecstatic Wind. In its thrall, seekers feel at one with the Anima Mundi: an orgasmic and spiritual rapture. In fact, the mage is losing her self-identity; her individuality bleeds away in the Wind. Inexperienced Awakened confuse the experience for Supernal Ascension, go mad, lose their humanity or simply starve to death in the Anima Mundi\u2019s unmediated embrace. In a small number of cases, Ecstatic Winds feel like a cold, killing force instead. Mysterium dream scholars believe that this is a manifestation of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the mage's Gnosis and her understanding of the Astral Plane confers a measure of protection against it. The more enlightened his Awakened soul is, and the better her handle on transcendental reality, the less likely the Wind affects her. Whenever she would take damage from the Ecstatic Wind, roll the mage's base Paradox pool. Each success inflicts damage to the Awakened charcter, in addition to the damage rating based on the Ecstatic Wind's strength.<br /> ' <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Location</b></u></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Typical Wind Strength</b></u></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Damage</b></u></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Interval</b></u></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Omphalos, Swath, Spire Perilous</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weak</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1L</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Every 24 Hours</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The Dreaming Earth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Medium</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2L</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Every Hour</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The Sidereal Wastes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Strong</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3L</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Every Turn*</td> </tr> </table></div> * - That is, every discrete action within the Sidereal Waste\u2019s multiple subjective time streams.<br /> <br /> If the mage is killed by Ecstatic Wind, she returns with the Soul Shocked Condition and loses a Willpower <i>dot</i> due to depersonalization. Since her soul momentarily escapes its usual confines of self to be smeared across raw celestial Being, she also brings back some sign of its deformity: a Paradox Condition (Mage 2nd Edition, p.116). This crosses metaphysical lines and can even affect the mage\u2019s physical body and surroundings. The Condition resolves itself as usual.<br /> <br /> ---=---<br /> <br /> <u><b>Amnion</b></u><br /> The Amnion is an intensified self-image that a sorcerer can invoke to protect herself. It takes many shapes, from antique diving suits to scaled hides and spiked bat\u2019s wings. Often, a given Amnion is based on a mage\u2019s nimbus, beliefs and personal history.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer may invoke her Amnion as an instant action. When she does so, she gains general armor equal to the lower of her Gnosis or highest subtle Arcanum against attacks that appear physical, and against the Ecstatic Wind. However, as a refined form of egocentrism, it impairs the ability to interact with the outside world, imposing a \u20132 die penalty to Finesse-based tasks and a \u20131 penalty to Defense. The Amnion is treated as a form of equipment. It doesn\u2019t stack with \u201cphysical\u201d armor, but does stack with spells and Attainments.<br /> <br /> The Ecstatic Wind weakens Amnia over time; the stronger it is, the faster an Amnion fades. After the mage has rolled for damage from the Wind, reduce the Amnion's armor by -1. If this would reduce it to 0, she may spend Mana (to invoke Supernal authority) or Willpower (to concentrate her own ego) to renew it.<br /> <br /> Mages can also dismiss their own Amnia. Several have been known to take this risk, particularly when local entities demand it. Amnia dull the full glory of the Anima Mundi by design, so mages sometimes risk greater exposure to better study the Dreamtime and perceive the full presence of their hosts. The alien majesty of the region is still incompatible with the human psyche, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-13-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T03:45:44-08:00","id":1047638,"title":"","content":"Just a small adjustment to the Ecstatic Wind's mechanics to better fit with my Mage House Rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T09:38:27-08:00","id":1047741,"title":"","content":"How's the Amnion fit into this? Or have you simply done away with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:02:15-08:00","id":1047963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule?p=1047741#post1047741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How's the Amnion fit into this? Or have you simply done away with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll need to look through the mechanics for it, again. I like the concept behind the Amnion, though, and I've even been thinking of doing a couple of Merits tied to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added a section on it to the opening post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-13-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T02:17:50-08:00","id":1050920,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Embracing the Wind</u></b><br /> While the Awakened must journey to the Anima Mundi using their Oneiroi as starting points, the Begotten have an easier time accessing it. Certain Pathways in the Dark Dream are resonant to the other Astral Realms, and a Beast can travel through some of them to reach the soul of the universe. However, they are more adversely affected by the Ecstatic Wind than mages are. The Dreamtime cares little for whatever stories and mythologies of humankind. It embodies the mortals' thoughts and fears of the world, and even Beasts have much cause to fear the world around them.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, Beasts <i>can</i> incorporate the Wind into their Lairs by forming Chambers tied to parts of the Anima Mundi. By doing so, they not only become immune to its effects, but can also summon it against their unsuspecting foes. Awakened characters are especially susceptible, as their enlightened souls intensify the effects of the Wind on them.<br /> <br /> --=--<br /> <br /> <b>New Trait -- Ecstatic Wind [Major]</b><br /> The Lair sings with the Dreamtime's power, and it can tear apart even those who arrive through their dreams. Whenever this Trait is imposed, treat it as an Extreme Environment whose level is half the Beast's Lair, rounded up, to a maximum of four. Mages also roll for additional damage (as per the rules for the Ecstatic Wind), while ephemeral and dream entities are affected as if the environment was one level less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-18-2017, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:58:29-08:00","id":1050950,"title":"","content":"Why would Beasts necessarily get stronger in the World Soul, though? They're still of humanity, reflecting what humans think and fear about the world, rather than being the world.<br /> <br /> Still, the idea of Beasts braving the Dreamtime despite all that and expanding their Lairs to it has an appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:14:37-08:00","id":1050958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule?p=1050950#post1050950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Beasts necessarily get stronger in the World Soul, though? They're still of humanity, reflecting what humans think and fear about the world, rather than being the world.<br /> <br /> Still, the idea of Beasts braving the Dreamtime despite all that and expanding their Lairs to it has an appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was somewhat inspired by the fact that werewolves in the Anima Mundi get +2 to Size and Strength on their Urshul and Urhan forms (as mentioned in the Astral Realms blue book). Seeing as they are of the Astral Realms, I find it rather logical that Beasts are empowered by being in the World Soul. It's also why they can invoke the Amnion like mages do.<br /> <br /> And yeah, drawing aspects of the Dreamtime for their Lairs <i>is</i> an appealing concept, especially since the Ecstatic Wind can be harnessed <i>outside</i> of it by the Begotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:28:25-08:00","id":1050964,"title":"","content":"Beasts are, in fact, hurt by being in the Anima Mundi more than mages are, as shown in the Beast Anthology. Rules for their version of the ecstatic wind are going to be in the Beast Player's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:32:18-08:00","id":1050965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule?p=1050964#post1050964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are, in fact, hurt by being in the Anima Mundi more than mages are, as shown in the Beast Anthology. Rules for their version of the ecstatic wind are going to be in the Beast Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh. Thanks for the heads up.<br /> <br /> When can we expect that book to come out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:33:35-08:00","id":1050967,"title":"","content":"Beasts are native to the Astral... but not the entire place. The Primordial Dream is still a part of the Temenos. The Anima Mundi should be frightening to them as well, since it doesn't care about whatever stories and mythologies humans make up about the world.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:49:07-08:00","id":1050971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule?p=1050967#post1050967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are native to the Astral... but not the entire place. The Primordial Dream is still a part of the Temenos. The Anima Mundi should be frightening to them as well, since it doesn't care about whatever stories and mythologies humans make up about the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited that segment to reflect that. Looking forward to getting that Player's Guide when it comes out so I can refine it further.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T21:47:39-07:00","id":1204789,"title":"","content":"Seeing as the Beast Player's Guide is out now, does anyone know what the Wind does to Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T22:10:24-07:00","id":1204791,"title":"","content":"Remember it doing damage scaling with Lair similar to how it scales with Gnosis. Will have to check later, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T03:47:03-07:00","id":1204826,"title":"","content":"It's mostly the same as mages, but it doesn't differ by region of the Anima Mundi (no safe areas for them) and if killed by the wind they lose Chambers out of their Lair rather than have a Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> The BPG doesn't just cover beasts in the AM: due to the game's crossoveriness it says what happens to all major templates. Werewolves have it easiest, Prometheans the worst, and Demons easy until it suddenly and horrifcally isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:53:08-07:00","id":1204865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047633-the-ecstatic-wind-house-rule?p=1204826#post1204826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly the same as mages, but it doesn't differ by region of the Anima Mundi (no safe areas for them) and if killed by the wind they lose Chambers out of their Lair rather than have a Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> The BPG doesn't just cover beasts in the AM: due to the game's crossoveriness it says what happens to all major templates. Werewolves have it easiest, Prometheans the worst, and Demons easy until it suddenly and horrifcally isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading something about animal shapeshifters along with werewolves - are they Changing Breeds, Skinchangers, Shapechangers etc from 1E books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:43:05-07:00","id":1204875,"title":"","content":"Since i have recently purchased the book in question, I have a question: \u2018Progenitor-Beasts\u2019 of the Mother\u2019s Land\u2014-are they basically just ancient Unfettered, or are they Incarnate Beasts of extreme age and power? Or are they something else, entirely? And are there \u2018Progenitor-Insatiables\u2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T09:28:48-07:00","id":1204883,"title":"","content":"They're Beast Aeons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}]